      "goals": {
        "en": "@ Develop research questions and design an experimental approach for  tackling these research questions\n@ Identify logical fallacies\n@ Formulate logical arguments using evidence-based reasoning \n@ Read and interpret scientific literature\n@ Practice communicating science (oral, visual and particularly in written formats)\n@ Design, perform and then interpret basic statistical analyses\n@ Provide critical feedback on scientific texts",
        "nl": ""
      },
      "description": {
        "en": "In this course, students will learn how to formulate a research plan by investigating various current topics in marine biology. They will then find  the forefront of their chosen field, develop a research question, and  design an approach for tackling their question. In practical workshops, students will practice analyzing experimental data. Using the skills\nthey develop, they will then predict the results of their experiments and explore the societal relevance of their topic.\nThey will combine these skills in a written research plan and then practice providing critical and constructive feedback to one another in  peer feedback sessions. The course culminates with presentations of each research plan, allowing students to practice oral and visual communication skills.",
        "nl": ""
      },
